WEBVTT

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:08.780
I have some food for you guys, too.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.730
H-Hey, guys-

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.870
She's fuming.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.130
Even the corporal's late; that sure is rare.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:43.630
Corporal-

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.120
Good mor-
Corporal-

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:44.650
Good mor-

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.840
Wait, huh?

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.860
Umm...

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.860
I found this lying there.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.530
I-Is it a suspicious item?

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.080
No, it's not a bomb.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.420
See?

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.820
...a bomb would've been easier to deal with than this...

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.320
Yeah...

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.510
Sergeant Major Oreld.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.790
It's been how many times now
that you've been tardy this month?

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.580
Umm...

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.800
Five... no, six...

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.370
Soldiers need to be punctual!

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.430
State your reason.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:33.160
Are you... sure you want me to?

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:39.320
People jeer us as a cheery unit
exactly because of these things!

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.210
Let us recite now...

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:43.680
...regarding the proper manner
in which we need to portray ourselves!

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.100
All men, repeat after me!

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.990
Us, too?

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.330
I guess.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.340
Three, and...

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.330
"We are..."

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.820
BOOBS!

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:57.620
Ah, 2nd Lieutenant!

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.000
Give me your boobs.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.250
A baby!

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.060
What in the world...

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.350
He's so cute!

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:15.020
Is he an abandoned baby?

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.220
His name is Dieter.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:20.830
Says here to "raise him to be a formidable soldier".

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.110
But they can't...

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.400
I see.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:28.330
Currently, people are saying that the places that have money right now are the military facilities.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.430
So, because of the harsh living conditions,

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:34.330
the mother couldn't raise him anymore and had to abandon him, I guess.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:39.290
Call this a "tragedy that was caused by the era".

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.540
Quit joking around!

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:42.840
Do you think it's all right for babies to be abandoned because their parents had no choice?

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.410
Blaming it on the era, or calling it inevitable...

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.660
...those are nothing but excuses!

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:53.200
We need to restore society back to the stage where parents can't use inevitability as an excuse to throw away children!

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.290
H-Hey!

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.110
Toddler, why are you crying?

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.690
Have I said something to offend you?

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.390
Hey, say something!

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:07.400
What's wrong?

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.660
Just hold him.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:10.880
Hold him?

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:14.480
He most likely wants to see mama and is crying because of that.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.590
Hold him and he'll stop crying.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:18.110
His mother, huh?

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.490
That's more like kite flying...

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:25.910
Now, now, toddler.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:26.680
Don't worry.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.310
Your mother may not be here,

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:32.310
but at least you're in Section III's hospitality, right?

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.440
He hasn't stopped crying even after I hugged him.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.030
Now this is funny...

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.480
Hey, that's not polite, Oreld.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:52.780
Alice, let me handle this!

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:56.580
You need to inject a lot of love when handling babies.

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:59.080
Hello, you lil' cherub~

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.150
Chuu~ chuu~

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.720
Huh, that's weird...

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:08.980
See, it's oneechan~

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.180
Cute lil' baby~

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:15.300
Love, love, cheek, cheek~

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.210
Master Sergeant, the way to show love is...

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:23.760
Sleep~ sleep~

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:27.170
Inside Mother's...

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:32.250
Sleep~! Sleep~!

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:36.420
Inside Mother's arms...

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.260
How come...

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:41.740
How come he hasn't stopped crying?

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:45.190
Could be hungry or a wet diaper,

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:47.010
one or the other, probably.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.750
Very perceptive.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.780
You sure are familiar with babies.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:53.040
He just drank some milk, right?

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.040
I bet he probably peed in his diapers.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.960
Yo, kid, go change his diapers.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.720
But he's a guy.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.750
Yeah, perfect lesson for you, right?

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:06.480
N-No! You take care of this, Oreld!

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:08.390
Me?

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.490
Okay.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.000
Machs, do something!!!

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.710
Big guy...

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.730
You picked him up; show some responsibility...

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.280
Oh...

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:38.900
What's this?

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:41.920
Did Section III start a daycare center now?

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:43.330
Oh, that's perfect.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.970
It's the most fitting mission for the cheery unit.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:49.790
Are you saying you don't sell milk or diapers?

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:51.440
Obviously!

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:53.950
What kind of store do you think this place is?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:58.480
But, all kinds of daily necessities should be available-

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:00.530
Telling me that isn't going to help.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:03.690
Besides, why is a baby here?

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:07.460
Babies can appear in military facilities; that happens!

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:09.080
See, there's one right here!

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:12.080
No, they usually don't...

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:14.740
Now you've surprised me.

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:15.920
Huh?

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:17.830
Is this your child?

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.630
N-No, it isn't!

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:20.560
Telling me that isn't going to help.
N-No, it isn't!

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.330
Telling me that isn't going to help.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:21.790
Sleeping all peacefully...

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:23.200
Shall I contact stores inside the city?
Sleeping all peacefully...

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.190
Shall I contact stores inside the city?

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:25.410
Okay.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:26.060
Do you have experience in raising children?
Okay.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.440
You'd help us a lot if you could do that.
Do you have experience in raising children?

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:27.780
You'd help us a lot if you could do that.

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:28.770
No...

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:32.080
Could I... hold him for a bit?

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:33.520
Yeah.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.410
He's gorgeous.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.780
Looks like he only wants to be in papa's arms.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:45.790
Papa?

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:47.920
Hmm, hmm...

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.890
Drip the warm milk onto your wrist to check the temperature.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:55.390
How long do you plan on holding him?

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:56.560
Oh...

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.130
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:00.990
He'll start crying right after the corporal lets go of him.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.430
Even so, I can't accept this!

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:06.810
Why would he only stop crying
when the corporal is holding him?

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:11.650
To be held by a woman like me should feel a lot better!

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.270
You think?

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:14.320
It must be!

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.400
Oh, it might be imprinting.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:20.280
So, the first one to find him was the corporal,

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:22.190
and he mistook him for his parent.

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:24.320
He's not a duckling...

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:29.260
Heck, it could be that big guy is his real parent!

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:30.150
Eh?

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.420
Is that true?

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.800
Of course not.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:35.800
He doesn't look like the corporal at all.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:38.220
Wait, don't tell me...

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:40.960
Is he really your child?

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.550
Of course not...

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.690
Y-Yeah...

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:49.690
So, what are we going to do about him?

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:53.330
We can't keep him forever.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:54.940
Yes, we know, but...

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.000
Either we bring him to a proper facility or...

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:01.070
Because at this rate, he might hinder our work.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.160
I'll go search.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.190
I'll go search for his mother.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:06.570
Are you serious?

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:10.810
It's unforgivable for a mother to throw away a child she endured so much pain to give birth to!

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:13.690
I will find this mother even if I have to look under every stone...

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:16.260
...and knock some sense into her imprudence!

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.950
Imprudence, huh?

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:22.590
That doesn't sound too bad.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.720
All right.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.350
Permission for your search mission granted.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.230
Boss!

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:32.590
We got piles of work to do,
and you're telling us to find an abandoned child's parent?

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:35.810
Hey, this is war relief, too.

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:36.860
What...

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.150
Don't be slacking, eh?

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:42.210
But...

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:43.880
What?

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:45.040
What now?

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:47.760
I think he wants to pee.

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:49.410
Well, carry him to the bathroom already!

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:55.210
Looks like he's really taken a liking to you, Corporal.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:11:02.300
There, there...

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:17.570
LT...

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:21.550
Do you plan on picking out
the baby's mother from all the people here?

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.010
Of course.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:29.100
A sentry soldier saw a suspicious woman in front of HQ disappearing towards the black market this morning.

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:32.520
He clearly remembers the clothing and the stature of the woman, too.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:34.850
Is that our only source?

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.350
Better than nothing.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:41.910
Wait.

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:43.450
Imperial S.S. III here.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:44.930
We need some information.

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:49.710
And how may I help you elites from the army?

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:51.500
We're looking for a woman.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:56.020
Have you seen a young woman
holding a basket containing a baby?

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.770
I don't know.

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:01.560
She wore a black shawl and has a thin build.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:04.190
Like I just said, I don't know.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:05.780
What about you?

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:08.020
We're looking for a child's mother.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:12.750
Anything would help.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.520
Please tell me if you know anything.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:17.790
Let's go.

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:20.580
These people really don't know about it.

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:22.580
Get your hands off.

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:23.570
I'm not done-

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:24.550
LT!

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:26.750
Look around you.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:31.120
We're interfering with business.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:34.950
After eating baby food...

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.940
Hmm, how many months old is Dieter-chan?

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:45.110
There, there, there...

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:52.200
Well, just give up and keep on holding him, Papa.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:56.080
How uncooperative of these people!

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.280
They should be ashamed!

00:12:57.280 --> 00:13:00.440
People here have tight lips.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:03.120
We're only here to look for a baby's mother.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.680
Why is it necessary to keep that a secret?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.780
They're all suspicious.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:11.440
Everyone here is treading dangerous waters.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:12.990
Dangerous waters?

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:14.260
In times like this,

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:16.800
if you try to live without breaking any laws,

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.130
you won't get any business done.

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:21.270
Are you saying they're committing crimes?

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:26.010
No laws govern this place!

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.230
If you say something offensive,

00:13:28.230 --> 00:13:31.680
we aren't guaranteed to live even if we're soldiers.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:33.180
That's foolish.

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:36.750
Do you think I fear the blades of the criminals?

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.000
I don't; that's why I'm worried.

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:43.180
Anyway, just leave things around here to me.

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:48.030
It'll take us forever if we just ask one stand at a time.

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:54.600
Aren't these army goods sold through illegal channels?

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.230
What?!

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:57.960
Now, stay calm...

00:13:57.960 --> 00:14:01.430
It's more important to find the baby's mother right now, right?

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.900
What do soldiers want from here?

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:10.700
Long time no see, pops.

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:16.370
Oreld?

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:21.120
Looks like the rumor about you joining the army was true.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.030
Well, sign of the times.

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:23.730
They know each other?
Well, sign of the times.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:23.900
They know each other?

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:24.840
Yeah.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:28.880
And, what do you want?

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:31.180
We're actually looking for someone,

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:33.060
and I thought you might know something, pops-

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.700
I don't, actually.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:39.060
Oh, don't worry, we're not looking for anyone suspicious.

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:41.570
It's a mother of an abandoned baby we're looking for.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.570
Abandoned baby?

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:46.730
A baby was left in front of the gates of HQ this morning.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:49.590
Would you happen to know something about it?

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:55.450
I don't think I have anything to say to people from the army.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:57.680
You guys are interfering with my business.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.430
Just go home, will ya?

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:00.960
Anything is fine.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.960
Can you tell us anything?

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:04.240
Who're you?

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.530
We're from the Imperial S.S. III.

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:08.550
We request your cooperation.

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:10.670
Imperial S.S. III?

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:13.680
Now, this is funny!

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:18.760
Oreld, you were assigned to the cheery unit?

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.020
Why you...

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.900
LT, let me handle things here.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:24.190
LT?

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.670
This little girl here?

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:30.370
Oreld... you've totally become a loser now...

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:32.770
Before, you were a wretched guy.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:35.660
Now, you're letting a girl like her drag your nose around.

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:37.240
Pops...

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.600
How about it?

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:41.320
Do you have any intentions of coming back to this town?

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:47.000
You entered the army,
but you got thrown into a useless unit...

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.520
How dare you call us useless!

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:53.010
Under the name of war relief, we, the Imperial S.S. III,

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:58.200
work day and night to expedite the process
of getting all civilians out of the war disasters-

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:02.030
You said you were looking for
the mother of an abandoned child, right?

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:03.040
Correct.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:04.270
How ridiculous.

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:07.980
Hearing this "war relief" thing makes me even sicker.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:12.210
Don't feel like you've accomplished something by doing just that.

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:16.900
This town is filled with
abandoned children and war orphans.

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:21.450
Are you telling me you're going to take care of all of them?!

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:24.560
Huh, LT?!

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.720
Why don't you cut it out already?

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:36.300
What did you just say?

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:40.050
We took a modest approach, and you get all cocky?

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:45.350
Stop saying all this bullshit and spill what you know already!!

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:48.780
Interesting... you brat...

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:51.480
You can talk pretty big, too, huh?

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:10.000
Trying to take me on? Come back in ten years!

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:18.520
Well, looks like you guys know where I come from now.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.430
There's nothing we can do?

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:27.940
We accomplished nothing, huh.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.480
Don't let your spirits down.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:35.010
Hey, you're not going to drink your juice?

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:37.080
You're not going to drink it?

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:39.830
No...

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.440
Then, can I have it?

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:43.000
C'mon, please!

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:43.900
Please!

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:45.410
S-Sure...

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.710
All right!

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:50.460
Yum!

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.530
Thanks, oichan!

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:53.460
Oichan?

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:54.910
See?

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:58.240
They all grow up strong even if they don't have parents.

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.460
I'm sure that baby will be the same, too.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:02.550
Okay.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:03.890
Are we going back?

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:06.020
We're going to search another round!

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:08.990
Oh... I see...

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.350
God...

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:13.970
My legs are dead...

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:17.030
And? No results?

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.660
Oh, where's the baby by the way?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.250
He started making noises again,

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:23.410
so the corporal took him out for a walk.

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:25.770
Poor corporal...

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:29.250
Hey, he brought it on himself.

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:32.600
I think we had way more trouble, though.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:36.920
I'm definitely going to feel muscle aches tomorrow.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:50.020
He finally went to sleep.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:55.980
Babies sure are cute.

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:57.360
Yes.

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:02.620
I couldn't find his mother.

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:05.040
It can't be helped.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:09.310
But, there are numerous children
that have lost their parents to the war.

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:13.940
Helping this one child out isn't going to change anything.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:15.630
Lieutenant...

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:20.220
Even I know that much, at least...

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:24.350
But now that I have seen this child,

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:28.060
I can't just walk away from him now.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:31.680
That's...

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:34.400
Hey!

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:38.950
Your baby's waiting for you!

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:42.460
You're Dieter's mother, right?

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.990
My husband was a smuggler.

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:58.910
He had no choice...

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:04.030
My husband came back from the war and didn't have a job...

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:07.060
That was the only thing he could do to help us survive.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:09.410
Why did you throw away your child?

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.570
You can't say it?

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:17.850
On a train inspection, the smuggled goods were found.

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:20.010
He got arrested, right?

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:24.560
And with the two of us left,

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:27.550
I didn't know what I should do.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:31.010
Rather than having me raise him,

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:35.190
I thought he'd be more fortunate for the army to raise him...

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:36.630
That's absurd!

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:39.420
Did you really think that was the right thing to do?!

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.240
Did you really think he'd be more fortunate like that?!

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:45.570
I'm sorry...

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:50.720
I did such a horrible thing to this child...

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:53.600
But...

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:56.400
You came to see this child...

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:03.400
Dieter...

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:07.470
Forgive me.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:15.160
As a member of Section III,
I cannot guarantee the both of you a happy life.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:20.040
But, this I promise you.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:24.010
I will make this society into a place
where happiness isn't an extravagance.

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:35.700
I ended up forgiving her since she was crying,

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.520
but that was different.

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:41.290
She wasn't apologizing to us,

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:44.610
but rather, to the baby.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:56.280
I wanted... to hug the baby one more time...

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.980
Mer-kun, the 2nd lieutenant is going to see her fiancee!

00:23:33.980 --> 00:23:35.360
It's so mind-boggling!

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:36.850
Huh? This guy?

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:39.600
How... weird...

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:42.330
Next time, "Dancers: The Lead and The Follow".

00:23:42.330 --> 00:23:44.450
Come get us if you're not scared!
